### ==============================================================================
### Gosmart.Health GRAPHITE - Administrative & Authentication Requests
### ==============================================================================
### Host variables are defined in .vscode/settings.json ("$shared" / "local" / "docker")
### You can switch environments via VS Code status bar (bottom right: Rest Client Env)

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. Authenticate Admin (Login to acquire JWT Tokens)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name login
POST {{graphServer}}/api/v1/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{adminUsername}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. Extract Token Variables (or use {{login.response.body.*}} directly)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@authToken = {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. Inspect System Metadata (Protected Admin Endpoint)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{graphServer}}/api/v1/system HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. Query DICOM Configurations
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{graphServer}}/api/v1/configurations/dicom HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. Refresh Access Token
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name refreshToken
POST {{graphServer}}/api/v1/auth/refresh HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "{{login.response.body.refresh_token}}"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. Create API Key for MCP / Programmatic Agents
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{graphServer}}/api/v1/auth/api-keys HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "user_id": "{{login.response.body.user.id}}",
  "name": "Local Agent Key",
  "scopes": ["*"]
}